<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khassonke</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khassonké</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khassonke are a people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayes">Kayes</a> region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, living along the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal-river">Senegal River</a>. They descend from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fula</a> herders who settled among Malinke farmers and adopted much of their culture, and their language, Khassonke, is a Mande language close to Malinke. In the 18th and 19th centuries they formed the Kingdom of Khasso.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khassonke.jpg" alt="Khassonke" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Famille.lecamus · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khassonkes.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
